  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...A couple more rounds of frost and freeze \nimpacts are expected both tonight and Sunday night where the \ngrowing season continues.\n\nLittle change in the overall synoptic pattern is expected\nthrough tonight with strong surface high pressure essentially\noverhead. In fact, 500 mb temperatures are a touch cooler \ntonight but surface dewpoints are expected to be a couple of \ndegrees higher tonight. Overall, this should result in low \ntemperatures pretty similar to those observed earlier this \nmorning with lows mainly in the low to mid 30s across the \nregion, outside of the barrier islands and coastal Delaware.\n\nFrost Advisories were upgraded to Freeze Warnings for portions\nof central and southern New Jersey. Dewpoints have trended a bit\nlower ahead of the sea breeze in this corridor where\ntemperatures are more prone to falling below a consensus of\nguidance. Skies will be more pristinely clear tonight with calm\nwinds, unlike the scattered to broken cirrus we had in place \nlast night, so opted to nudge temperatures down another degree \nor two into the low 30s. This justifies the warning upgrade for \nthe aforementioned areas. Elsewhere, Frost Advisories remain in \nplace for tonight where the growing season remains active (along\nand SE of I-95). The exception is for the barrier islands of NJ\nand coastal DE, which should experience lows in the 40s again. \nWould not be surprised to see some areas dip into the upper 20s,\nmore notably across the Pine Barrens of South Jersey and \nsheltered valleys of NW NJ and the southern Poconos.\n\nTemperatures will then begin to moderate on Sunday before\nanother round of frost is possible for Sunday night into Monday\nmorning. Lows around the region will mainly be in the mid 30s to\nlow 40s. Depending on how tonight's frost advisories pan out\nwill determine where frost advisories may be warranted on Sunday\nnight...more details to come in future updates.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Water levels are decreasing and remaining Coastal Flood\nAdvisories have been cancelled. Spotty minor tidal flooding may\nlinger through daytime Sunday.\n\nWater levels are continuing to decrease in the back bay areas \nof Ocean County, NJ and Sussex County, Delaware and no further\nwidespread tidal flooding is expected. As a result, the Coastal\nFlood Advisory for these counties has been cancelled. Spotty\nminor tidal flooding may linger in the back bays though over the\nnext two high tide cycles, through daytime Sunday.",
